1
00:00:10,439 --> 00:00:14,840
Good morning," said the little prince.

2
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:23,039
"Good morning to you said the railway switchman please tell me What do you do here?"

3
00:00:23,039 --> 00:00:26,039
the little prince asked.

4
00:00:26,039 --> 00:00:31,560
"I saw out Travelers in bundles of a thousand," said the switchman

5
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:37,319
and I said and off the trains that carry him now to the right, now to the left."

6
00:00:37,319 --> 00:00:42,060
And a brilliantly lighted express train shook the switchman's cabin as it rushed

7
00:00:42,060 --> 00:00:45,719
by with a roar like thunder.

8
00:00:45,719 --> 00:00:50,399
"They are in a great hurry," said the little prince.

9
00:00:50,399 --> 00:00:52,800
"What are they looking for?"

10
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:58,139
"Not even the locomotive engineer knows that," said the switchman.

11
00:00:58,139 --> 00:01:04,560
And a second brilliantly lighted express thundered by, in the opposite direction.

12
00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:06,800
"Are they coming back already?"

13
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:09,479
demanded the little prince.

14
00:01:09,479 --> 00:01:16,020
"These are not the same ones," said the switchman. "It is an exchange."

15
00:01:16,020 --> 00:01:19,198
"Were they not satisfied where they were?"

16
00:01:19,198 --> 00:01:21,600
asked the little prince.

17
00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:27,060
"No one is ever satisfied where he is," said the switchman. And they heard the

18
00:01:27,060 --> 00:01:32,340
roaring thunder of a third brilliantly lighted express.

19
00:01:32,340 --> 00:01:38,639
"Are they pursuing the first Travelers demanded the little prince.

20
00:01:38,639 --> 00:01:43,439
"They are pursuing nothing at all," said the switchman.

21
00:01:43,439 --> 00:01:48,300
"They are asleep in there, or if they're not asleep they are yawning.

22
00:01:48,300 --> 00:01:53,399
Only the children are flattening their noses against the window panes

23
00:01:53,399 --> 00:01:58,738
Only the children know what they are looking for the little prince.

24
00:01:58,738 --> 00:02:03,600
"They waste their time over a ragdoll and it becomes very important to them;

25
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:09,618
and if anybody takes it away from them, they cry..."

26
00:02:09,618 --> 00:02:15,920
"They are lucky," the switchman said
